---
source: crates/odx-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_long_help().to_string()
---
Copy exact pins (and optionally code) of modules or a feature between environments

Usage: odx promote [OPTIONS] --to <ENV> [MODULES]...

Arguments:
  [MODULES]...
          Modules to promote, with their dependency closure

Options:
  -C, --project-dir <DIR>
          Run as if started in DIR

      --from-pr <N>
          Promote the project addons a pull request merged into the source changed

  -c, --config <FILE>
          The pyproject.toml or repos.yaml to use

      --rollback <N>
          Revert the promotion pull request N merged into --to

      --feature <NAME>
          Promote a feature set from [tool.odx.features]

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Override the number of parallel jobs

      --offline
          Serve forge and index data from the cache only. Only network calls are skipped: local work (git, pre-commit, odoo-lint) takes as long as before

      --search <TEXT>
          Find modules and feature sets by functional description; lists candidates

      --fresh
          Ignore cached data; refresh everything before answering

      --select <NAMES>
          The candidates of --search to promote

      --from <ENV>
          Source environment [default: the one environment allowed to promote into --to]

      --no-refresh
          Use cached data even when stale. Like --offline, this saves network time only

      --refresh-index
          Rebuild the addon index for the series involved

      --to <ENV>
          Target environment

      --json
          Machine-readable output on stdout

      --remote <NAME>
          The remote whose branches are read (local branches when it has none)
          
          [default: origin]

      --allow-downgrade
          Copy an older package over a newer one

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (repeatable)

      --allow-source-change
          Replace an addon that comes from another source on the target

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only

      --no-with-odoo
          Leave the Odoo core revision of the target as it is

      --with-code
          Cherry-pick the source's commits on the closure's project addons that the target lacks

      --allow-transitive
          Keep what `uv lock` re-resolves outside the closure

      --include-branch-specific <PATH>
          Also copy this branch-specific file or folder (repeat per path)

      --commit
          Write the plan as a commit on `odx/promote/<to>-<selection>`

      --open-pr
          Commit, push the branch and open its pull request

      --yes
          Confirm writing (with --commit or --open-pr)

  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version
